IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc5-s110-4-to-117.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada): PART III (Firearms and Other Weapons), the second half of the run that begins in ccc4's range:
-- sections 110.4 to 117 (the hearing after an emergency prohibition order, the prohibition order, revocation, lifting for sustenance or employment,
-- surrender, forfeiture, revocation of authorizations, return to owner). Layer 1: the law, objectively. Provisions that address a judge, a justice or an
-- officer are encoded for what they decide about the person the order is made against. Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the
-- Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text.
-- Answers are MAYBE BOOLEAN (JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / NOTHING) or a core type. JUST FALSE only where the text says no in its own words; NOTHING otherwise.
-- Seams: `s 110.1 an emergency prohibition order has been made` (MAYBE BOOLEAN, from ccc4); `s 2 ...` terms as MAYBE BOOLEAN; `Part XXVII ...` (from ccc29).

§ `Part III continued -- orders prohibiting possession (ss 110.4 to 117)`

§§ `s 110.4 Order under subsection 111(5)`

-- src:2383 | 110.4 (1) If a provincial court judge makes an order under subsection 110.1(3), the judge may, on the judge’s own motion, fix a date for the hearing of an application made under subsection 111(1) and shall direct that notice of the hearing be given, in the manner that the judge may specify, to the person against whom an order under subsection 111(5) is sought.
@ref s 110.4(1) (src:2383)
GIVEN `s 110.1 an emergency prohibition order has been made` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 110.4(1) the provincial court judge may fix a date for the hearing of an application under subsection 111(1)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`s 110.1 an emergency prohibition order has been made` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2383 | 110.4 (1) If a provincial court judge makes an order under subsection 110.1(3), the judge may, on the judge’s own motion, fix a date for the hearing of an application made under subsection 111(1) and shall direct that notice of the hearing be given, in the manner that the judge may specify, to the person against whom an order under subsection 111(5) is sought.
@ref s 110.4(1) (src:2383)
GIVEN `s 110.1 an emergency prohibition order has been made` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the judge has fixed a date for the hearing of an application made under subsection 111(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 110.4(1) the provincial court judge is bound to direct that notice of the hearing be given to the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`s 110.1 an emergency prohibition order has been made` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `the judge has fixed a date for the hearing of an application made under subsection 111(1)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a provincial court judge makes an order under subsection 110.1(3)"

-- src:2385 | (2) For the purpose of this section,
-- src:2386 | (a) the application for the order referred to in subsection 110.1(3) is deemed, except for the purpose of subsection 111(2), to be an application made under subsection 111(1); and
@ref s 110.4(2)(a) (src:2385-2386)
GIVEN `the application is the application for the order referred to in subsection 110.1(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is the purpose of subsection 111(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 110.4(2)(a) the application for the order under subsection 110.1(3) is deemed an application made under subsection 111(1)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the purpose is the purpose of subsection 111(2)` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except for the purpose of subsection 111(2)"
        IF `the application is the application for the order referred to in subsection 110.1(3)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)


-- src:2385 | (2) For the purpose of this section,
-- src:2387 | (b) if a person other than a peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer made the application for the order referred to in subsection 110.1(3), the Attorney General of the province in which the application was made — or, if the application was made in a territory, the Attorney General of Canada — becomes the applicant, in their place, in the application made under subsection 111(1).
@ref s 110.4(2)(b) (src:2385-2387)
GIVEN `the application was made by a person other than a peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `where the application was made` IS A `Province or territory`
GIVETH A MAYBE Party
`s 110.4(2)(b) the Attorney General who becomes the applicant` MEANS
    IF `the application was made by a person other than a peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer`
    THEN CONSIDER `where the application was made`
         WHEN Yukon THEN JUST `the Attorney General of Canada`
         WHEN `Northwest Territories` THEN JUST `the Attorney General of Canada`
         WHEN Nunavut THEN JUST `the Attorney General of Canada`
         OTHERWISE JUST `the Attorney General or Solicitor General of the province`
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if a person other than a peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer made the application"


-- src:2389 | (3) The date fixed for the hearing must be before the end of the period for which the order made under subsection 110.1(3) is in force. However, a provincial court judge may, before or at any time during the hearing, on application by the applicant or the person against whom an order under subsection 111(5) is sought, adjourn the hearing.
@ref s 110.4(3) (src:2389)
GIVEN `the date fixed for the hearing` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the period for which the order made under subsection 110.1(3) is in force ends` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 110.4(3) the date fixed for the hearing is before the end of the period of the order` MEANS
    IF `the date fixed for the hearing` LESS THAN `the day on which the period for which the order made under subsection 110.1(3) is in force ends`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be before the end of the period for which the order made under subsection 110.1(3) is in force"

-- src:2389 | (3) The date fixed for the hearing must be before the end of the period for which the order made under subsection 110.1(3) is in force. However, a provincial court judge may, before or at any time during the hearing, on application by the applicant or the person against whom an order under subsection 111(5) is sought, adjourn the hearing.
@ref s 110.4(3) (src:2389)
GIVEN `the application to adjourn is made by the applicant or by the person against whom an order under subsection 111(5) is sought` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made before or at any time during the hearing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 110.4(3) the provincial court judge may adjourn the hearing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the application to adjourn is made by the applicant or by the person against whom an order under subsection 111(5) is sought` AND `the application is made before or at any time during the hearing` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "before or at any time during the hearing, on application by the applicant or the person against whom an order under subsection 111(5) is sought"

-- src:2391 | (4) If the Attorney General becomes, under paragraph (2)(b), the applicant in an application made under subsection 111(1), the provincial court judge shall, as soon as feasible but not later than 15 days before the date fixed under subsection (1), cause notice of that application and of that date to be served on that Attorney General.
@ref s 110.4(4) (src:2391)
GIVEN `the Attorney General becomes, under paragraph (2)(b), the applicant in an application made under subsection 111(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 110.4(4) the provincial court judge is bound to cause notice to be served on the Attorney General` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Attorney General becomes, under paragraph (2)(b), the applicant in an application made under subsection 111(1)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the Attorney General becomes, under paragraph (2)(b), the applicant"


-- src:2391 | (4) If the Attorney General becomes, under paragraph (2)(b), the applicant in an application made under subsection 111(1), the provincial court judge shall, as soon as feasible but not later than 15 days before the date fixed under subsection (1), cause notice of that application and of that date to be served on that Attorney General.
@ref s 110.4(4) (src:2391)
GIVEN `the date on which notice was served on the Attorney General` IS A DATE
      `the date fixed under subsection (1)` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 110.4(4) the notice was served not later than 15 days before the date fixed` MEANS
    IF `the date on which notice was served on the Attorney General` AT MOST `the date fixed under subsection (1)` MINUS 15
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "not later than 15 days before the date fixed"

-- The same duty as a regulative rule. The clock counts days from the day the date was fixed; the deadline is the 15th day before the date fixed.
-- "as soon as feasible" is a judgment with no number in the text, so only the outer limit is run (NOTES.md, fork register).
DECLARE `s 110.4(4) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 110.4(4) cause notice to be served on the Attorney General`

@ref s 110.4(4) (src:2391)
GIVEN `the number of days from the day the date was fixed to the date fixed for the hearing` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 110.4(4) act`
`s 110.4(4) the judge must cause notice to be served on the Attorney General` MEANS
    PARTY `a provincial court judge`
    MUST `s 110.4(4) cause notice to be served on the Attorney General`
    WITHIN (`the number of days from the day the date was fixed to the date fixed for the hearing` MINUS 15)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `a provincial court judge` BECAUSE "notice was not served on the Attorney General at least 15 days before the date fixed"

-- src:2393 | (5) If a provincial court judge revokes an order made under subsection 110.1(3) against a person before the application for an order sought under subsection 111(5) against the person is heard, the judge shall cancel the hearing.
@ref s 110.4(5) (src:2393)
GIVEN `the judge revokes an order made under subsection 110.1(3) against the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application for an order sought under subsection 111(5) against the person has not yet been heard` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 110.4(5) the provincial court judge is bound to cancel the hearing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the judge revokes an order made under subsection 110.1(3) against the person` AND `the application for an order sought under subsection 111(5) against the person has not yet been heard` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a provincial court judge revokes an order made under subsection 110.1(3)"

§§ `s 111 Application for prohibition order`

-- src:2395 | 111 (1) A peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer may apply to a provincial court judge for an order prohibiting a person from possessing any firearm, cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance, or all such things, if the peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer believes on reasonable grounds that it is not desirable in the interests of the safety of the person against whom the order is sought or of any other person that the person against whom the order is sought should possess any such thing.
@ref s 111(1) (src:2395)
GIVEN `s 2 peace officer: the applicant is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is a firearms officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is a chief firearms officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant believes on reasonable grounds that it is not desirable in the interests of the safety of the person against whom the order is sought or of any other person that the person against whom the order is sought should possess any such thing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 111(1) a peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer may apply to a provincial court judge for an order prohibiting a person from possessing weapons` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF ((`s 2 peace officer: the applicant is one` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR `the applicant is a firearms officer` OR `the applicant is a chief firearms officer`) AND `the applicant believes on reasonable grounds that it is not desirable in the interests of the safety of the person against whom the order is sought or of any other person that the person against whom the order is sought should possess any such thing` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2397 | (2) On receipt of an application made under subsection (1), the provincial court judge shall fix a date for the hearing of the application and direct that notice of the hearing be given, in such manner as the provincial court judge may specify, to the person against whom the order is sought.
@ref s 111(2) (src:2397)
GIVEN `an application has been made under subsection 111(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 111(2) the provincial court judge is bound to fix a date for the hearing and direct that notice be given to the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `an application has been made under subsection 111(1)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On receipt of an application made under subsection (1)"

-- src:2399 | (3) Subject to subsection (4), at the hearing of an application made under subsection (1), the provincial court judge shall hear all relevant evidence presented by or on behalf of the applicant and the person against whom the order is sought.
@ref s 111(3) (src:2399)
GIVEN `the hearing of an application made under subsection 111(1) is held` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge proceeds ex parte under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 111(3) the provincial court judge is bound to hear all relevant evidence presented by or on behalf of the applicant and the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the hearing of an application made under subsection 111(1) is held` AND (NOT `the judge proceeds ex parte under subsection (4)`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2401 | (4) A provincial court judge may proceed ex parte to hear and determine an application made under subsection (1) in the absence of the person against whom the order is sought in the same circumstances as those in which a summary conviction court may, under Part XXVII, proceed with a trial in the absence of the defendant.
@ref s 111(4) (src:2401)
GIVEN `the application is made under subsection 111(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person against whom the order is sought is absent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Part XXVII the circumstances are those in which a summary conviction court may proceed with a trial in the absence of the defendant` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 111(4) the provincial court judge may proceed ex parte to hear and determine the application` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the application is made under subsection 111(1)` AND `the person against whom the order is sought is absent` AND (`Part XXVII the circumstances are those in which a summary conviction court may proceed with a trial in the absence of the defendant` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2403 | (5) If, at the conclusion of a hearing of an application made under subsection (1), the provincial court judge is satisfied that the circumstances referred to in that subsection exist, the provincial court judge shall make an order prohibiting the person from possessing any firearm, cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance, or all such things, for the period, not exceeding five years, that is specified in the order, beginning on the day on which the order is made.
@ref s 111(5) (src:2403)
GIVEN `the hearing of an application made under subsection (1) has concluded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied that the circumstances referred to in subsection (1) exist` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 111(5) the provincial court judge is bound to make an order prohibiting the person from possessing the things` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the hearing of an application made under subsection (1) has concluded` AND `the judge is satisfied that the circumstances referred to in subsection (1) exist` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If, at the conclusion of a hearing of an application made under subsection (1), the provincial court judge is satisfied that the circumstances referred to in that subsection exist"


-- src:2403 | (5) If, at the conclusion of a hearing of an application made under subsection (1), the provincial court judge is satisfied that the circumstances referred to in that subsection exist, the provincial court judge shall make an order prohibiting the person from possessing any firearm, cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance, or all such things, for the period, not exceeding five years, that is specified in the order, beginning on the day on which the order is made.
@ref s 111(5) (src:2403)
GIVEN period IS A `Length of time`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 111(5) the period of the order is not more than five years` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF period's years TIMES 12 PLUS period's months LESS THAN 60 THEN JUST TRUE
        IF period's years TIMES 12 PLUS period's months EQUALS 60 AND period's days EQUALS 0 THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for the period, not exceeding five years"

@ref s 111(5) (src:2403)
GIVEN `the day on which the order is made` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the period begins` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 111(5) the order begins on the day on which it is made` MEANS
    IF `the day on which the period begins` EQUALS `the day on which the order is made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "beginning on the day on which the order is made"

-- src:2405 | (6) Where a provincial court judge does not make an order under subsection (1), or where a provincial court judge does make such an order but does not prohibit the possession of everything referred to in that subsection, the provincial court judge shall include in the record a statement of the court’s reasons.
@ref s 111(6) (src:2405)
GIVEN `the judge does not make an order under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge makes an order but does not prohibit the possession of everything referred to in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 111(6) the provincial court judge is bound to include a statement of reasons in the record` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the judge does not make an order under subsection (1)` OR `the judge makes an order but does not prohibit the possession of everything referred to in subsection (1)`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a provincial court judge does not make an order under subsection (1)"


-- src:2407 | (7) Sections 113 to 117 apply in respect of every order made under subsection (5).
@ref s 111(7) (src:2407)
GIVEN `the order is made under subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision` IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 111(7) sections 113 to 117 apply to the order, tested by section number` MEANS
    IF `the order is made under subsection (5)` AND `the provision`'s `section` AT LEAST 113 AND `the provision`'s `section` AT MOST 117
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Sections 113 to 117 apply in respect of every order made under subsection (5)"

-- src:2409 | (8) Where a provincial court judge makes an order under subsection (5), the person to whom the order relates, or the Attorney General, may appeal to the superior court against the order.
@ref s 111(8) (src:2409)
GIVEN `the appellant is the person to whom the order relates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appellant is the Attorney General` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provincial court judge makes an order under subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 111(8) the person to whom the order relates, or the Attorney General, may appeal to the superior court against the order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the provincial court judge makes an order under subsection (5)`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a provincial court judge makes an order under subsection (5)"
        IF (`the appellant is the person to whom the order relates` OR `the appellant is the Attorney General`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2411 | (9) Where a provincial court judge does not make an order under subsection (5), the Attorney General may appeal to the superior court against the decision not to make an order.
@ref s 111(9) (src:2411)
GIVEN `the appellant is the Attorney General` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provincial court judge does not make an order under subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 111(9) the Attorney General may appeal to the superior court against the decision not to make an order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the provincial court judge does not make an order under subsection (5)`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a provincial court judge does not make an order under subsection (5)"
        IF `the appellant is the Attorney General` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)


-- src:2413 | (10) The provisions of Part XXVII, except sections 785 to 812, 816 to 819 and 829 to 838, apply in respect of an appeal made under subsection (8) or (9), with such modifications as the circumstances require and as if each reference in that Part to the appeal court were a reference to the superior court.
@ref s 111(10) (src:2413)
GIVEN `the section of Part XXVII in question` IS A NUMBER
      `the provision is a provision of Part XXVII` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal is made under subsection (8) or (9)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 111(10) the provision of Part XXVII applies to the appeal` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the section of Part XXVII in question` AT LEAST 785 AND `the section of Part XXVII in question` AT MOST 812) OR (`the section of Part XXVII in question` AT LEAST 816 AND `the section of Part XXVII in question` AT MOST 819) OR (`the section of Part XXVII in question` AT LEAST 829 AND `the section of Part XXVII in question` AT MOST 838) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except sections 785 to 812, 816 to 819 and 829 to 838"
        IF `the provision is a provision of Part XXVII` AND `the appeal is made under subsection (8) or (9)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): only an appeal made under subsection (8) or (9) is reached

§§ `s 112 Revocation of prohibition order under subsection 110.1(3) or 111(5)`

-- src:2416 | 112 A provincial court judge may, on application by the person against whom an order is made under subsection 110.1(3) or 111(5), revoke the order if satisfied that the circumstances for which it was made have ceased to exist.
@ref s 112 (src:2416)
GIVEN `the application is made by the person against whom an order is made under subsection 110.1(3) or 111(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied that the circumstances for which the order was made have ceased to exist` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 112 a provincial court judge may revoke the order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the application is made by the person against whom an order is made under subsection 110.1(3) or 111(5)`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on application by the person against whom an order is made under subsection 110.1(3) or 111(5)"
        IF `the judge is satisfied that the circumstances for which the order was made have ceased to exist` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

§§ `s 113 Lifting of prohibition order for sustenance or employment`

-- src:2418 | 113 (1) Where a person who is or will be a person against whom a prohibition order is made establishes to the satisfaction of a competent authority that
-- src:2419 | (a) the person needs a firearm or restricted weapon to hunt or trap in order to sustain the person or the person’s family, or
-- src:2420 | (b) a prohibition order against the person would constitute a virtual prohibition against employment in the only vocation open to the person,
-- src:2421 | the competent authority may, notwithstanding that the person is or will be subject to a prohibition order, make an order authorizing a chief firearms officer or the Registrar to issue, in accordance with such terms and conditions as the competent authority considers appropriate, an authorization, a licence or a registration certificate, as the case may be, to the person for sustenance or employment purposes.
@ref s 113(1) (src:2418-2421)
GIVEN `the person is or will be a person against whom a prohibition order is made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person establishes to the satisfaction of the competent authority that the person needs a firearm or restricted weapon to hunt or trap in order to sustain the person or the person's family` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person establishes to the satisfaction of the competent authority that a prohibition order against the person would constitute a virtual prohibition against employment in the only vocation open to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 113(1) the competent authority may make an order authorizing a licence, authorization or registration certificate for sustenance or employment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is or will be a person against whom a prohibition order is made` AND (`the person establishes to the satisfaction of the competent authority that the person needs a firearm or restricted weapon to hunt or trap in order to sustain the person or the person's family` OR `the person establishes to the satisfaction of the competent authority that a prohibition order against the person would constitute a virtual prohibition against employment in the only vocation open to the person`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person who is or will be a person against whom a prohibition order is made establishes to the satisfaction of a competent authority that"

-- src:2423 | (2) A competent authority may make an order under subsection (1) only after taking the following factors into account:
-- src:2424 | (a) the criminal record, if any, of the person;
-- src:2425 | (b) the nature and circumstances of the offence, if any, in respect of which the prohibition order was or will be made; and
-- src:2426 | (c) the safety of the person and of other persons.
@ref s 113(2) (src:2423-2426)
GIVEN `the competent authority has taken into account the criminal record, if any, of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the competent authority has taken into account the nature and circumstances of the offence, if any, in respect of which the prohibition order was or will be made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the competent authority has taken into account the safety of the person and of other persons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 113(2) the competent authority may make an order under subsection (1) only after taking the factors into account` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the competent authority has taken into account the criminal record, if any, of the person` AND `the competent authority has taken into account the nature and circumstances of the offence, if any, in respect of which the prohibition order was or will be made` AND `the competent authority has taken into account the safety of the person and of other persons` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only after taking the following factors into account"

-- src:2428 | (3) Where an order is made under subsection (1),
-- src:2429 | (a) an authorization, a licence or a registration certificate may not be denied to the person in respect of whom the order was made solely on the basis of a prohibition order against the person or the commission of an offence in respect of which a prohibition order was made against the person; and
@ref s 113(3)(a) (src:2428-2429)
GIVEN `the denial is solely on the basis of a prohibition order against the person or the commission of an offence in respect of which a prohibition order was made against the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an order is made under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 113(3)(a) an authorization, licence or registration certificate is barred from being denied solely on the basis of the prohibition order or the offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `an order is made under subsection (1)`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an order is made under subsection (1)"
        IF `the denial is solely on the basis of a prohibition order against the person or the commission of an offence in respect of which a prohibition order was made against the person` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2428 | (3) Where an order is made under subsection (1),
-- src:2430 | (b) an authorization and a licence may, for the duration of the order, be issued to the person in respect of whom the order was made only for sustenance or employment purposes and, where the order sets out terms and conditions, only in accordance with those terms and conditions, but, for greater certainty, the authorization or licence may also be subject to terms and conditions set by the chief firearms officer that are not inconsistent with the purpose for which it is issued and any terms and conditions set out in the order.
@ref s 113(3)(b) (src:2428-2430)
GIVEN `an order is made under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authorization or licence is issued for sustenance or employment purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order sets out terms and conditions and the issue is not in accordance with them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 113(3)(b) the authorization or licence may be issued to the person for the duration of the order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the authorization or licence is issued for sustenance or employment purposes`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only for sustenance or employment purposes"
        IF `the order sets out terms and conditions and the issue is not in accordance with them` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only in accordance with those terms and conditions"
        IF `an order is made under subsection (1)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an order is made under subsection (1)"

-- src:2430 | (b) an authorization and a licence may, for the duration of the order, be issued to the person in respect of whom the order was made only for sustenance or employment purposes and, where the order sets out terms and conditions, only in accordance with those terms and conditions, but, for greater certainty, the authorization or licence may also be subject to terms and conditions set by the chief firearms officer that are not inconsistent with the purpose for which it is issued and any terms and conditions set out in the order.
@ref s 113(3)(b) (src:2430)
GIVEN `the further terms and conditions are not inconsistent with the purpose for which the authorization or licence is issued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the further terms and conditions are not inconsistent with any terms and conditions set out in the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 113(3)(b) the chief firearms officer may attach further terms and conditions to the authorization or licence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the further terms and conditions are not inconsistent with the purpose for which the authorization or licence is issued` AND `the further terms and conditions are not inconsistent with any terms and conditions set out in the order` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2432 | (4) For greater certainty, an order under subsection (1) may be made during proceedings for an order under subsection 109(1), 110(1), 110.1(3), 111(5), 117.05(4) or 515(2), paragraph 732.1(3)(d) or section 810 or 810.03.
@ref s 113(4) (src:2432)
GIVEN `the proceedings are for an order under subsection 109(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are for an order under subsection 110(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are for an order under subsection 110.1(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are for an order under subsection 111(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are for an order under subsection 117.05(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are for an order under subsection 515(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are for an order under paragraph 732.1(3)(d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are for an order under section 810` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are for an order under section 810.03` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 113(4) an order under subsection (1) may be made during the proceedings` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the proceedings are for an order under subsection 109(1)` OR `the proceedings are for an order under subsection 110(1)` OR `the proceedings are for an order under subsection 110.1(3)` OR `the proceedings are for an order under subsection 111(5)` OR `the proceedings are for an order under subsection 117.05(4)` OR `the proceedings are for an order under subsection 515(2)` OR `the proceedings are for an order under paragraph 732.1(3)(d)` OR `the proceedings are for an order under section 810` OR `the proceedings are for an order under section 810.03`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed)

-- src:2434 | (5) In this section, competent authority means the competent authority that made or has jurisdiction to make the prohibition order.
@ref s 113(5) (src:2434)
GIVEN `the authority made the prohibition order or has jurisdiction to make it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 113(5) competent authority` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the authority made the prohibition order or has jurisdiction to make it` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means the competent authority that made or has jurisdiction to make the prohibition order"

§§ `s 114 Requirement to surrender`

-- src:2436 | 114 A competent authority that makes a prohibition order against a person may, in the order, require the person to surrender to a peace officer, a firearms officer or a chief firearms officer
-- src:2437 | (a) any thing the possession of which is prohibited by the order that is in the possession of the person on the commencement of the order, and
-- src:2438 | (b) every authorization, licence and registration certificate relating to any thing the possession of which is prohibited by the order that is held by the person on the commencement of the order,
@ref s 114 (src:2436-2438)
GIVEN `the authority makes a prohibition order against the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is in the person's possession on the commencement of the order and its possession is prohibited by the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authorization, licence or registration certificate relates to a thing the possession of which is prohibited by the order and is held by the person on the commencement of the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 114 the competent authority may require the person to surrender the things and documents` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the authority makes a prohibition order against the person` AND (`the thing is in the person's possession on the commencement of the order and its possession is prohibited by the order` OR `the authorization, licence or registration certificate relates to a thing the possession of which is prohibited by the order and is held by the person on the commencement of the order`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2436 | 114 A competent authority that makes a prohibition order against a person may, in the order, require the person to surrender to a peace officer, a firearms officer or a chief firearms officer
-- src:2439 | and where the competent authority does so, it shall specify in the order a reasonable period for surrendering such things and documents and during which section 117.01 does not apply to that person.
@ref s 114 (src:2436-2439)
GIVEN `the authority requires the person in the order to surrender things or documents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 114 the authority is bound to specify in the order a reasonable period for surrendering` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the authority requires the person in the order to surrender things or documents` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the competent authority does so"

-- src:2436 | 114 A competent authority that makes a prohibition order against a person may, in the order, require the person to surrender to a peace officer, a firearms officer or a chief firearms officer
-- src:2439 | and where the competent authority does so, it shall specify in the order a reasonable period for surrendering such things and documents and during which section 117.01 does not apply to that person.
@ref s 114 (src:2436-2439)
GIVEN `the order requires the person to surrender things or documents and specifies a reasonable period for it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day is within the period specified in the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 114 section 117.01 does not apply to the person during the specified period` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the order requires the person to surrender things or documents and specifies a reasonable period for it` AND `the day is within the period specified in the order` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "during which section 117.01 does not apply to that person"

§§ `s 115 Forfeiture`

-- src:2443 | (1.1) Subsection (1) does not apply in respect of an order made under subsection 110.1(3) or section 515.
@ref s 115(1.1) (src:2443)
GIVEN `the order is made under subsection 110.1(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order is made under section 515` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 115(1.1) subsection (1) does not apply to the order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the order is made under subsection 110.1(3)` OR `the order is made under section 515`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2441 | 115 (1) Unless a prohibition order against a person specifies otherwise, every thing the possession of which is prohibited by the order is forfeited to Her Majesty if, on the commencement of the order, the thing is in the person’s possession or has been seized and detained by, or surrendered to, a peace officer.
-- src:2443 | (1.1) Subsection (1) does not apply in respect of an order made under subsection 110.1(3) or section 515.
@ref s 115(1) (src:2441-2443)
GIVEN `the thing is one the possession of which is prohibited by the prohibition order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `on the commencement of the order the thing is in the person's possession` IS A BOOLEAN
      `on the commencement of the order the thing has been seized and detained by, or surrendered to, a peace officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prohibition order specifies otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 115(1.1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 115(1) the thing is forfeited to Her Majesty` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the prohibition order specifies otherwise` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless a prohibition order against a person specifies otherwise"
        IF (`the answer of s 115(1.1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not apply"
        IF `the thing is one the possession of which is prohibited by the prohibition order` AND (`on the commencement of the order the thing is in the person's possession` OR `on the commencement of the order the thing has been seized and detained by, or surrendered to, a peace officer`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2445 | (2) Every thing forfeited to Her Majesty under subsection (1) shall be disposed of or otherwise dealt with as the Attorney General directs.
@ref s 115(2) (src:2445)
GIVEN `the thing is forfeited to Her Majesty under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 115(2) the thing forfeited is to be disposed of or otherwise dealt with as the Attorney General directs` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the thing is forfeited to Her Majesty under subsection (1)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

§§ `s 116 Authorizations revoked or amended`

-- src:2447 | 116 (1) Subject to subsection (2), every authorization, licence and registration certificate relating to any thing the possession of which is prohibited by a prohibition order and issued to a person against whom the prohibition order is made is, on the commencement of the prohibition order, revoked, or amended, as the case may be, to the extent of the prohibitions in the order.
@ref s 116(1) (src:2447)
GIVEN `the authorization, licence or registration certificate relates to a thing the possession of which is prohibited by the prohibition order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was issued to the person against whom the prohibition order is made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 116(1) the authorization, licence or registration certificate is revoked or amended on the commencement of the prohibition order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the authorization, licence or registration certificate relates to a thing the possession of which is prohibited by the prohibition order` AND `it was issued to the person against whom the prohibition order is made` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2449 | (2) An authorization, a licence and a registration certificate relating to a thing the possession of which is prohibited by an order made under subsection 110.1(3) or section 515 is revoked, or amended, as the case may be, only in respect of the period during which the order is in force.
@ref s 116(2) (src:2449)
GIVEN `the order is made under subsection 110.1(3) or section 515` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day is within the period during which the order is in force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 116(2) the authorization, licence or registration certificate remains revoked or amended` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the order is made under subsection 110.1(3) or section 515` AND `the day is within the period during which the order is in force` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only in respect of the period during which the order is in force"

§§ `s 117 Return to owner`

-- src:2451 | 117 Where the competent authority that makes a prohibition order or that would have had jurisdiction to make the order is, on application for an order under this section, satisfied that a person, other than the person against whom a prohibition order was or will be made,
-- src:2452 | (a) is the owner of any thing that is or may be forfeited to Her Majesty under subsection 115(1) and is lawfully entitled to possess it, and
-- src:2453 | (b) in the case of a prohibition order under subsection 109(1) or 110(1), had no reasonable grounds to believe that the thing would or might be used in the commission of the offence in respect of which the prohibition order was made,
-- src:2454 | the competent authority shall order that the thing be returned to the owner or the proceeds of any sale of the thing be paid to that owner or, if the thing was destroyed, that an amount equal to the value of the thing be paid to the owner.
@ref s 117 (src:2451-2454)
GIVEN `the authority is satisfied, on application for an order under this section, that a person other than the person against whom a prohibition order was or will be made applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the owner of a thing that is or may be forfeited to Her Majesty under subsection 115(1) and is lawfully entitled to possess it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prohibition order is an order under subsection 109(1) or 110(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person had no reasonable grounds to believe that the thing would or might be used in the commission of the offence in respect of which the prohibition order was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117 the competent authority is bound to order the thing returned to the owner, or its proceeds or value paid` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the authority is satisfied, on application for an order under this section, that a person other than the person against whom a prohibition order was or will be made applies` AND `the person is the owner of a thing that is or may be forfeited to Her Majesty under subsection 115(1) and is lawfully entitled to possess it` AND ((NOT `the prohibition order is an order under subsection 109(1) or 110(1)`) OR `the person had no reasonable grounds to believe that the thing would or might be used in the commission of the offence in respect of which the prohibition order was made`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on application for an order under this section, satisfied that a person"


-- src:2454 | the competent authority shall order that the thing be returned to the owner or the proceeds of any sale of the thing be paid to that owner or, if the thing was destroyed, that an amount equal to the value of the thing be paid to the owner.
@ref s 117 (src:2454)
DECLARE `s 117 state of the thing` IS ONE OF
    `s 117 the thing still exists`
    `s 117 the thing was sold`
    `s 117 the thing was destroyed`

DECLARE `s 117 order for the owner` IS ONE OF
    `s 117 the thing is returned to the owner`
    `s 117 the proceeds of the sale are paid to the owner`
    `s 117 an amount equal to the value of the thing is paid to the owner`

@ref s 117 (src:2454)
GIVEN state IS A `s 117 state of the thing`
GIVETH A `s 117 order for the owner`
`s 117 what the order for the owner is` MEANS
    CONSIDER state
    WHEN `s 117 the thing still exists` THEN `s 117 the thing is returned to the owner`
    WHEN `s 117 the thing was sold` THEN `s 117 the proceeds of the sale are paid to the owner`
    WHEN `s 117 the thing was destroyed` THEN `s 117 an amount equal to the value of the thing is paid to the owner`   -- "if the thing was destroyed"
